   "evidence": "Intro lemmas present: `pair` (:106), `cons` (:131), `sturmSeq` (:222); no `[p]` constructor. The singleton obligation is discharged inline inside `sturmSeq` at :233-236 (`have hi : i + 2 < 1 := by simpa using (List.getElem?_eq_some_iff.mp h2).1; omega`) and :237-240, duplicating the pattern already written for `pair` at :114-127 \u2014 evidence the obligation is non-obvious and recurring.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/Sturm/SignedRemainders.lean",
   "fix": "Add `theorem IsSignedRemainderSeq.singleton {p : R[X]} (hp : p \u2260 0) : IsSignedRemainderSeq [p]` and use it in `IsSignedRemainderSeq.sturmSeq`, replacing the inline proof at lines 231\u2013240.",
   "issue": "`IsSignedRemainderSeq` has intro forms `pair` ([p,q]), `cons` (\u22653 entries) and `sturmSeq`, but none for a singleton `[p]` \u2014 the case the public `sum_sign` (Tarski.lean:224, `cs = []`) and the PR description specifically support. A user must either reprove the vacuous `relation`/`terminal` fields via the `List.getElem?_eq_some_iff`/length-`omega` argument or route through `sturmSeq p 0` plus `sturmSeq_zero_right`.",
   "line": "106"
  },
  {
   "evidence": "`SignType.sign` needs only `[Zero \u03b1] [Preorder \u03b1] [DecidableLT \u03b1]` (mathlib/Mathlib/Basic/Sign/Defs.lean:266), all supplied by `LinearOrder`; the sibling definition `List.signVariations` with identical typeclasses is a plain `def` and is evaluated by `example : signVariations [1, 0, -2, 3, 3] = 2 := by decide` (mathlib/Mathlib/Data/List/SignVariations.lean:47-50).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Data/List/SignVariations.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `noncomputable` from `def firstSign`.",
   "issue": "`List.firstSign` is `noncomputable`, but with `[Zero R] [LinearOrder R]` its body (`List.filter` on a decidable predicate, `Option.map SignType.sign`, `getD`) is computable; the modifier forces `noncomputable` onto every downstream definition and rules out executable/`decide` use of this general list-level API.",
   "line": "23"
  }
